      "id": 5343,
      "name": "mrconner",
      "username": "mrconner",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/b3f665/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2011-11-23T02:16:16.000Z",
      "cooked": "<ol>\n<li>\n<p>If a card does damage damage to multiple targets, do you have to deal that damage?  i.e. Ball lightning where you might not want to deal lightning damage to a particular target.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>With an ongoing card that does damage at the start of a turn, can you choose not to deal that damage?  Our example is Impale played on Baron Blade when he has his Elemental Redistributer engaged - we’d prefer not to deal the cold damage as it would kill our weakest hero</p>\n</li>\n</ol>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:34:58.094Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
