      "id": 24135,
      "name": "TheJayMann",
      "username": "TheJayMann",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/thejaymann/{size}/2261_2.png",
      "created_at": "2011-11-23T13:30:03.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Hmm… the official ruling stated that heroes didn’t have to be targeted.  And, in the case where the number of non-hero targets is greater than or equal to the number of targets specified by X, then you don’t have to target a hero, unless you so desired.  Though, he wasn’t really specific enough as far as if you could choose not to satisfy the entire target count.  The question was asked again, more specifically asking about having to satisfy all targets (as the card does not say “up to”) and has not been answered yet.  If you don’t have to satisfy the entire target count, then the card is likely a “misprint” or sorts.</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
